post.description:
Replaces the person's recovery codes with a fresh set, shown this once;
every earlier code stops working. The person proves who they are again
first. Records `authentication.recovery_codes_generated`.

Returns `202` while the worker moves TLS from `Provisioning` to `Active`;
poll the domain for completion. `SelfManaged` uses HTTP-01 on its hostname;
`Delegated` uses DNS-01 in our zone, allowing automatic renewal and wildcards.
Requires `Domains(Update)`. Missing domains return `404`; unverified
domains or already-active certificates return `409`. Records
`tenant.domain_tls_requested`, then `tenant.domain_tls_provisioned` on issue.

get.description:
Every consent the user gave or withdrew, on every set of terms, with
when and where from. A person reads their own with their session;
anyone else needs the right to view users. Read-only.

The user's sign-ins and failed attempts, newest first, as the tenant's
audit trail recorded them. A person reads their own with their session;
anyone else needs the right to view users. Read-only.

api_key.description:
Optional API key: paste one to bring your own OpenAI or Anthropic;
leave it out for a keyless self-hosted endpoint. Encrypted at rest;
never returned.

IssueLdapCertificateBody.description:
Request body for issuing an LDAP client certificate.

`csr_pem` is a PEM-encoded PKCS#10 signing request made on the device;
the private key is never sent.

approval.description:
For a loop whose first step asks one approval for every item:
`waiting` while no pass may start, `given` once people approved;
left out for a loop that asks nobody about every item.
